# Production build config. Tracked in git on purpose: no secrets here, and CI
# needs it to produce the production bundle.
#
# VITE_APP_NAME and VITE_APP_URL are deliberately gone. One bundle serves every
# brand, so a baked-in name or app URL is wrong for all but one of them. Both
# now arrive at runtime from GET /embed/context.
#
# VITE_API_URL is left UNSET on purpose, which makes the widget call its own
# origin. That is what a per-brand-domain deployment needs: ai.salesplay.com
# talks to ai.salesplay.com, ai.sellmo.com talks to ai.sellmo.com, and several
# app instances sharing one database each talk to their own backend. It used to
# hardcode a single brand's domain, which would have sent every other brand's
# API calls there.
#
# It is still read, so set it when the API genuinely lives somewhere else --
# a dev box, a sandbox, or a frontend served from a different host than its
# backend:
#
#   VITE_API_URL=https://api.sandbox.example.com
#
# Leave it unset for any deployment where nginx serves the app and proxies
# /api/ on the same domain (see docs/multi-brand-deployment-runbook.md for the
# required location blocks -- the /api -> /v1 rewrite is not optional).
